<title>CHILE: Talks continuing at Quebrada Blanca - official.</title>
<headline>Talks continuing at Quebrada Blanca - official.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unions and management were in talks Wednesday morning at the Quebrada Blanca copper mine where a strike was due to start on the first shift Wednesday.</p>
<p>Asked whether the strike had started, a company official at the mine replied, &quot;No comment. As far as I know they are still negotiating.&quot;</p>
<p>About 300 miners at the mine voted Sunday to reject the company's pay offer and strike.</p>
<p>The mine, which produces 75,000 tons of copper cathodes a year, is owned by Canadian companies Cominco Ltd and Teck.</p>
</text>
